From efc0b9069c8e7d071299dd2cf88c0347ebda6166 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:08:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Curling: doubles, three and four teams, cups and the rink's
 own menu

A match can be a duel against a city recruit, doubles with a recruit as the mate, or three or four teams on the rink at once. The rink opens on a menu of its own: the mode, then a quick match against rivals drawn at random or one of five cups (Rookie, Amateur, Expert, Elite, Legend), each asking for its own fish, closed in grey until the cup before it is won and its four players live in the city, and marked with a trophy once won. A singles or doubles cup is a knockout of eight shown as a draw before each round; a free-for-all cup is three matches on points shown as a table. Cup progress is kept per mode in saved variables 7, 8 and 15. The classic match against Penguinmon or MetalMamemon is unchanged.
